    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [X] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.completion\n\n### Description\n\nhey,\r\nwhile configing `mini.files` found out that `mini.completion` could makes text lags to appear on screen, I recorded a video to show how easily it can be reproduced \r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/assets/27911493/43493a3b-919a-417f-bdb6-41692588c9cd\r\n\n\n### Neovim version\n\n0.9.5\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. open a file like this:\r\n```lua\r\nreturn {\r\n\t\"echasnovski/mini.files\",\r\n\tconfig = function()\r\n\t\trequire(\"mini.files\").setup()\r\n\t\tvim.keymap.set(\"n\", \"-\", \"<cmd>=MiniFiles.open()<CR>\")\r\n\r\n\t\tvim.api.nvim_create_autocmd(\"FileType\", {\r\n\t\t\tpattern = \"minifiles\",\r\n\t\t\t},\r\n\tend,\r\n}\r\n```\r\n2. move to `pattern` line and try to rapidly write `callback` and remove it letter by letter\r\n\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nHaving smooth typing experience \n\n### Actual behavior\n\nit's visible in recorded video.",
