            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Unfortunately, I can not reproduce this. The reproduction steps are not complete: in video you have autocompletion from 'lua/autocmd.lua' file with unknown content.\r\n\r\nI'd ask to make it indeed reproducible with only 'mini.completion' enabled and some known text in buffers opened.\r\n\r\n------\r\n\r\nHere is what I have:\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/assets/24854248/2e82ca7d-278e-4d0f-8cef-a9b1081065d1\r\n\r\n------\r\n\r\nThat said, if this comes from fallback built-in completion, it *might* have this effect if there is *some* buffer with *lots* of text to scan (like somewhere around 10000 lines). But it can be not this case, of course.",
