            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "So... I've done some testing. My current hypothesis is that this is a result of a default fallback action kicking in. The only way I can reproduce this is as following:\r\n- Type `ca` fast.\r\n- Make delay **just over 100 ms**, which is the default of `config.delay.completion`.\r\n- Type `ll` fast.\r\n\r\nWith these steps I can see similar drawing issues as in original video. I think I did not see it initially because I typed too fast thinking it was a performance issue.\r\n\r\n@mortezadadgar, I would like to ask you to confirm the hypothesis (at least to a certain degree) by setting `fallback_action = function() end` instead of `\"<C-n>\"` and trying to reproduce same drawing issues. With this, I could not reproduce.\r\n\r\n------\r\n\r\nIf no fallback action resolves the issues, then I am afraid nothing can be done here. Built-in completion is synchronous by its implementation and there is no reasonable way to go around that.",
