        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "On Neovim>=0.12 (current Nightly) it is possible to `vim.o.completetimeout = 100` to limit the time of how long `<C-n>` (default fallback action) takes to compute its candidates.\n\n~~Also, what 'mini.nvim' / 'mini.completion' version do you use? Is it `main` branch or 0.16?~~ I see that you use 0.16 version. There was eb4d6bd268f7168a8a0d187c93d5954d5ef93bfd after the 0.16 release which improves responsiveness of default fallback. What is the output of `:=vim.o.complete`? It should not contain the `t` flag.\n\n> ... the cursor moves to the command area, freezes and come back to the insert mode after about half a second.\n\nThis doesn't look like a behavior that comes from 'mini.completion'.",
